	<body>
		<div class="column">
			<a href="../../#extended-library">← back</a>
			<h1>Scotland the Brave</h1>

			<p>
				<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotland_the_Brave"
					>Scotland the Brave</a
				>
				is a traditional song celebrating Scotland's heritage, landscapes and spirit.
				You will often hear the bagpipe players performing this, especially the buskers
				on the royal mile of Edinburgh.
			</p>

			<YouTube
				id="xqeYKf8tdsU"
				title="SCOTLAND THE BRAVE | PIPES & DRUMS ( HD )"
			/>
			<YouTube
				id="inHpvMyAzFs"
				title="Scotland the Brave - Scottish Patriotic Song [LYRICS]"
			/>

			<img
				src="/castells-music/sheet music/Scotland the Brave/Scotland the Brave (1st Gralla) [solfege].svg"
				alt="Sheet music for Scotland the Brave"
			/>

			<ul>
				<li>
					1st voice:
					<a
						href="/castells-music/sheet music/Scotland the Brave/Scotland the Brave (1st Gralla) [solfege].pdf"
						>pdf</a
					> |
					<a
						href="/castells-music/sheet music/Scotland the Brave/Scotland the Brave (1st Gralla) [solfege, diagrams].pdf"
						>pdf with finger diagrams</a
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					2nd voice:
					<a
						href="/castells-music/sheet music/Scotland the Brave/Scotland the Brave (2nd Gralla) [solfege].pdf"
						>pdf</a
